{start_of_verse}
[D]Hold back the rushing minutes make the wind lie [G]still
[A7]Don’t let the moonlight shine across the lonely [D]hill
[D7]Dry all the raindrops and hold back the [G]sun
[A7]My world has ended my baby’s [D]gone
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
The [A7]milkman whistles softly as he [G]comes up to my [D]door
The [A7]mailman brings the letters by just [G]like he did [D]before
[D]They seem so busy all day long as [D7]though there’s nothing [G]wrong
Don’t they [A7]know the world has ended? My baby’s [D]gone
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
I [A7]wake up sometimes in the night and [G]realize you’re [D]gone
And [A7]then I toss upon my bed and [G]wait for day to [D]come
[D]I try to tell my lonely heart it [D7]must go on [G]alone
But it [A7]cries the world has ended, my baby’s [D]gone
{end_of_verse}
